---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About prism</h1>
    <p>
      A gallery of thirty components, built two a week over ninety days. Every one is plain
      HTML, CSS and vanilla JavaScript, so it drops into any page regardless of framework.
    </p>
    <h2>Why no literal colours</h2>
    <p>
      Components reference design tokens and nothing else. The palette is generated from an
      image: hue and chroma are read from the pixels, while lightness stays on a fixed ladder
      that the image never touches. That is what keeps contrast readable no matter which
      wallpaper you choose, and it is why the components survive being dropped into someone
      else's brand.
    </p>
    <h2>Why the prompts are here</h2>
    <p>
      Each component records the prompt that produced it, along with the earlier attempts that
      failed and the reason they failed. The code is the easy half. Knowing which constraints
      to state up front is the part worth keeping.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: 62ch; }
  .prose h1 { font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 34px); margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 19px; margin: 30px 0 8px; }
  .prose p { color: var(--text-dim); margin: 0 0 14px; }
</style>
